<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>ILLUSTRATIVE starlink-15-16 ascent (3DOF sim)</name><description>ILLUSTRATIVE ASCENT ECEF — Falcon 9 Starlink Group 15-16 (27 V2 Mini Optimized, SLC-4E) — NOT OFFICIAL TELEMETRY
Method: first-principles 3DOF sim (/workspace/trajectory-deck/sim/ascent3dof.py): WGS-84 rotating Earth, J2, US76 drag,
TIMELINE mode: every ignition/cutoff/separation/fairing time is a published hard event; mdot=F_vac/(Isp_vac*g0); thrust SL/vac on ambient pressure.
FITTED (least squares vs published knots): vertical rise 9.71 s, kick 3.496 deg over 10 s, Cd 0.400, payload 16899 kg,
gravity turn, then linear-tangent steering tan(theta)=0.4614-0.000985*(t-t_ign stage 1).
Vehicle config: SpaceX Falcon 9 Block 5 (reusable first stage, droneship recovery) — TIMELINE mode (sim/vehicles/falcon9.json; every number carries a source URL, derivation, or ASSUMPTION).
Falcon 9 Block 5 masses from Wikipedia &#x27;Falcon 9 Block 5&#x27; spec table; thrust/Isp from Wikipedia &#x27;Falcon 9&#x27; spec table (citing SpaceX).
TIMELINE mode (tuned 2026-10-25): MECO 146 s, stage sep 150 s, SES-1 156 s, fairing 176 s, SECO-1 (final cutoff) from SpaceX&#x27;s sl-15-16 timeline are hard events.
Throttle profile not published: full published thrust throughout; unburned stage-1 residual stands in for entry/landing propellant.
Not flown: LL2 NET 2026-10-27T07:25:51Z (Tue 27 Oct 12:25:51 am PDT; retimed 26 Oct from 04:45Z, then 05:46:37Z; LL2 Go, window end 08:45Z), status Go; Spaceflight Now agrees (B1082.26, OCISLY). File continues past SECO-1 through SES-2/SECO-2 to payload deploy (POST-CUTOFF lines).
Published timeline (SpaceX): Max-Q 1:08, MECO 2:26, stage sep 2:30, SES-1 2:36, fairing 2:56, SECO-1 8:39, SES-2 53:01, SECO-2 53:03, deploy 1:01:53.
Target orbit: SpaceX pre-launch state vector (CelesTrak SupGP starlink-g15-16): deploy 252 x 265 km, i 70.007 deg. CelesTrak SupGP re-checked 26 Oct 9:38 pm PDT for T0 07:25:51Z: elset epoch 05:59:40Z, shape unchanged (252.1 x 264.7 km, i 70.007); its RAAN 185.36 deg is 36.1 deg west of the sim's 221.5 deg, i.e. SpaceX's vector still corresponds to T0 ~04:57Z, not yet updated (noted).
Target (see launch config): insertion 159 km, apoapsis 265 km, fpa 0, launch azimuth 155.87 deg; payload 16899 kg.
Pad: 34.632000N -120.611000E. Frame: WGS-84 ECEF, positions km, velocities km/s (Earth-relative).
T0 used: 2026-10-27T07:25:51Z. Re-run with another T0 by shifting utc_iso only; ECEF geometry is Earth-fixed.
POST-CUTOFF: after final cutoff T+519.0 s the stage coasts (same WGS-84/J2/US76-drag model) to PAYLOAD DEPLOY T+3713 s; rows after cutoff tagged -coast/-burn.
POST-CUTOFF burn &#x27;SES-2/SECO-2 (MVac restart)&#x27;: ign T+3181.0 s, 2.0 s at 329.32 kN prograde (Isp 348 s); timing from SpaceX timeline; thrust solved (throttle unpublished) so the 2 s burn raises perigee to the SpaceX/CelesTrak deploy perigee 252.1 km.
POST-CUTOFF deploy T+3713 s (SpaceX sl-15-16 timeline: deploy T+01:01:53): alt 263.82 km, osculating 254.7 x 264.5 km, i 70.04 deg.
POST-CUTOFF note: CelesTrak SupGP (re-checked 26 Oct) epoch 05:59:40Z; pre-retime deploy-state epoch was T+3737 s, 24 s after SpaceX&#x27;s published deploy; SpaceX time used.
POST-CUTOFF note: Perigee/apogee are osculating (r - 6378.137 km) and will differ by a few km from CelesTrak mean elements.</description>
